=== WEB-PARITY READING (read end-to-end before writing) ===
LayoutBreadcrumbs.tsx is a 5-line composition:
    const overrides = useBreadcrumbOverrides();   // merged per-page label overrides (context)
    const items = useBreadcrumbs(overrides);        // resolve the trail for the current route
    return <Breadcrumbs items={items} />;           // render; self-suppresses when items.length <= 1
Branches that REALLY exist in the source (reproduced all; none skipped):
  • rendered  — a nested/detail route (> 1 trail item) draws the trail.
  • suppressed — a top-level page (single item; web `items.length <= 1 → null`) draws nothing.
  • empty     — an unknown/chrome-less route (web `useBreadcrumbs` returns `[]`) draws nothing.
Faithful-parity note on the generic state list (loading/error/stale/offline): the web composition
performs NO fetch and reads NO remote data (overrides live in React state; the route comes from the
in-memory router), so it has no loading/error/stale/offline branches. Inventing freshness chrome would
be drift (covenant 9), so — exactly as the sibling 0166 did — those are documented N/A and the three
real branches above are reproduced. The empty/suppressed branch renders an intentional zero-content,
accessibility-hidden slot (web returns null; the surrounding chrome row keeps its quick-search hint),
and the DEBUG inspector renders a friendly note for the non-drawing branches so previews/tests are
never a blank box.

